          'In December 2019, digging foundations for classrooms at Gia Thủy Primary School (now Gia Tường commune, Ninh Bình), an excavator exposed a brick tomb. The excavation of February 2020 showed it lay north - south with three chambers: a front one for offerings, a middle one, and a rear one for the dead. The walls are of rectangular bricks and the vault of wedge-shaped bricks. Archaeologists provisionally date it to the 3rd century.',
